body:
https://github.com/algolia/instantsearch.js/blob/fix/getRefinements-hierarchical/src/lib/utils.js#L134-L137

Basically, for

``` js
{
  name: 'myHierarchicalFacet',
  attributes: ['myHierarchicalFacet.lvl0', 'myHierarchicalFacet.lvl1', 'myHierarchicalFacet.lvl2'],
  separator: ' > '
}
```

and a refinement like this `Cat > SubCat`;
the hierarchical data returned by the helper looks like this:

``` js
{
  name: 'myHierarchicalFacet',
  data: [
    {
      name: 'Cat',
      count: 2,
      data: [
        { name: 'Subcat', count: 1 }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

This is really different from another type of facet where it is like this:

``` js
{
  name: 'myFacet',
  data: {
    Cat: 2
  }
}
```

Hence the need for a special handling.

